
<%- include('Partials/head') %>
<body>

<nav class="navbar">
    <a href="/" class="logo">EJS<span>.Learn</span></a>


<ul class="nav-links">
    <li><a href="/">Tags</a></li>
    <li><a href="/rand">Random</a></li>
</ul>


</nav>

<div class="container">


<section class="hero">
    <h1>EJS Tags</h1>
    <p>
        Learn how EJS tags work with simple examples and live output.
    </p>
</section>


<section class="section">

    <h2>&lt;% %&gt; — Scriptlet</h2>

    <p>
        The &lt;% %&gt; tag is called a Scriptlet tag. It is used to write
        and execute JavaScript code inside an EJS file. The JavaScript
        code runs on the server, but it does not directly produce output
        in the HTML page.
    </p>

    <div class="demo-card">

        <%
            let name = "Shresth";
            let age = 20;
        %>

        <p>Name: <%= name %></p>
        <p>Age: <%= age %></p>

    </div>

</section>


<section class="section">

    <h2>&lt;%= %&gt; — Output</h2>

    <p>
        The &lt;%= %&gt; tag outputs the value of a JavaScript variable
        or expression into the HTML page. EJS automatically HTML-escapes
        the value.
    </p>

    <div class="demo-card">

        <p>Hello, <%= name %>!</p>

        <%
            let message = "<strong>Hello</strong>";
        %>

        <div class="output">
            <%= message %>
        </div>

    </div>

</section>


<section class="section">

    <h2>&lt;%- %&gt; — Unescaped Output</h2>

    <p>
        The &lt;%- %&gt; tag outputs a value without HTML escaping.
        Therefore, HTML contained inside the value can be interpreted
        by the browser.
    </p>

    <div class="demo-card">

        <div class="output">
            <%- message %>
        </div>

    </div>

</section>


<section class="section">

    <h2>&lt;%# %&gt; — EJS Comment</h2>

    <p>
        The &lt;%# %&gt; tag creates an EJS comment. The content is
        ignored by EJS and does not appear in the generated HTML.
    </p>

</section>


<section class="section">

    <h2>&lt;%_ — Whitespace Slurping</h2>

    <p>
        The &lt;%_ tag works like a normal Scriptlet tag while also
        removing whitespace that appears immediately before it.
    </p>

    <div class="demo-card">

        <%
            let showMessage = true;
        %>

        <%_ if (showMessage) { %>
            <p>This message is visible.</p>
        <% } %>

    </div>

</section>


<section class="section">

    <h2>&lt;%% — Literal EJS Tag</h2>

    <p>
        The &lt;%% tag is used when you want to display the characters
        &lt;% literally instead of having EJS interpret them.
    </p>

    <div class="demo-card">

        <p>
            Example: &lt;%%
        </p>

    </div>

</section>


<section class="section">

    <h2>%&gt; — Normal Ending</h2>

    <p>
        The %&gt; tag normally closes an EJS Scriptlet and returns the
        template to normal HTML.
    </p>

    <div class="demo-card">

        <%
            let x = 10;
        %>

        <p>X = <%= x %></p>

    </div>

</section>


<section class="section">

    <h2>-%&gt; — Newline Slurping</h2>

    <p>
        The -%&gt; tag removes the newline immediately following the
        EJS tag.
    </p>

    <div class="demo-card">

        <ul>
            <% if (true) { -%>
                <li>Item 1</li>
                <li>Item 2</li>
            <% } -%>
        </ul>

    </div>

</section>


<section class="section">

    <h2>_%&gt; — Whitespace Slurping</h2>

    <p>
        The _%&gt; tag removes whitespace appearing after the EJS tag.
        It gives you more control over spaces and newlines in the
        generated HTML.
    </p>

    <div class="demo-card">

        <% if (true) { _%>
            <p>This message is visible.</p>
        <% } %>

    </div>

</section>


</div>

<footer>
    EJS Learning Project • Built with Express + EJS
</footer>

</body>
</html>
